{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Until this day.</b> These are the words of HaShem, which He would say and Moses would write — and so too the preceding verses, ״וַיָּמָת שָׁם מֹשֶׁה״, ״וַיִּקְבֹּר אֹתוֹ״." "<b>And I saw</b> in the Rav, Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra, who wrote that Joshua wrote these. But it is not fitting to write such things in the plain sense of the verses, [implying] that Moses did not complete the scroll of the Torah that he handed over to the Levites, for in my ears I have heard from members of our people entangling themselves in this matter and branching off from it into heresy regarding the Torah — and this is precisely the claim of the nations, that members of Israel edited the text, so that what was not [there] is found in it and what was [there] is not found in it. May these words and their like sink away; turn your eyes away from them. The fundamental principle is that Moses wrote the entire scroll of the Torah, as they said (Bava Batra 15a): he completed it with tears."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:34.638987894Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}